---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
const title = "How to Remove Duplicate Lines from a List - Toolkit Lab";
const description = "How to remove repeated lines from a list or spreadsheet column, ignore case and extra spaces, and sort the result.";
---
<Base title={title} description={description} path="/guides/how-to-remove-duplicate-lines-from-a-list.html">
  <aside class="ad-rail" aria-label="Advertisement"><div class="ad-slot ad-slot-rail"></div></aside>
  <div class="wrap article">
    <p class="note"><a href="/guides.html">Guides</a> / Text cleanup</p>
    <h1>How to Remove Duplicate Lines from a List</h1>
    <p class="lead">Mailing lists, keyword lists and imported data often contain repeated entries. Removing duplicates before you use the list avoids sending the same message twice or counting items more than once.</p>
    <div class="ad-slot" aria-label="Advertisement"></div>
<h2>Why duplicates appear</h2>
<p>Lists are often merged from several sources, and the same item can appear with different capital letters or extra spaces. A simple comparison treats apple and Apple as different, so these need handling first.</p>
<h2>Steps</h2>
<ol>
<li>Paste the list with one item per line.</li>
<li>Turn on ignore case and ignore surrounding spaces if the list may contain those differences.</li>
<li>Press the button. The first occurrence of each item is kept, and later copies are removed.</li>
<li>Sort the result if you want it in alphabetical order.</li>
</ol>
<h2>Check the result</h2>
<p>Compare the counts shown. If far more lines were removed than you expected, check whether the ignore case setting merged items that should stay separate.</p>
<h2>Try it yourself</h2>
<p>The <a href="/tools/remove-duplicate-lines.html">Remove Duplicate Lines</a> tool does this in your browser. Your list is not saved or sent anywhere.</p>
      <section class="worked">
        <h2>Worked example</h2>
        <p>A list of apple, Banana, apple, banana, cherry with ignore case on: the second apple and the second banana match earlier lines, so the result is apple, Banana, cherry. Three lines remain from five, and two duplicates are removed.</p>
      </section>
      <section class="faq-list">
        <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
        <details><summary>Which copy is kept?</summary><p>The first occurrence of each line stays in its original position, and later copies are removed.</p></details>
        <details><summary>Should I turn off ignore case?</summary><p>Turn it off if capital letters mean something different in your list, such as product codes that differ only by case.</p></details>
        <details><summary>Can I sort the list?</summary><p>Yes. Tick Sort A to Z to put the cleaned list in alphabetical order after the duplicates are removed.</p></details>
      </section>
      <script is:inline type="application/ld+json">{"@context": "https://schema.org", "@type": "FAQPage", "mainEntity": [{"@type": "Question", "name": "Which copy is kept?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "The first occurrence of each line stays in its original position, and later copies are removed."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "Should I turn off ignore case?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Turn it off if capital letters mean something different in your list, such as product codes that differ only by case."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "Can I sort the list?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Yes. Tick Sort A to Z to put the cleaned list in alphabetical order after the duplicates are removed."}}]}</script>
